---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import Button from '../../components/ui/Button.astro';

const breadcrumbs = [{ name: 'Academics', href: '/academics/' }];
---

<PageLayout
  title="Curriculum & Academic Pedagogy"
  description="Comprehensive CBSE curriculum from Nursery to Class XII incorporating the XSEED 5-step experiential method in primary years and integrated competitive coaching in senior years."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
>
  <div class="space-y-16 max-w-5xl mx-auto">
    <!-- Overview Intro -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-10 items-center">
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-bold text-crimson-900 leading-tight">
          Nurturing Inquiring Minds and Confident Problem Solvers
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-paper-700 leading-relaxed">
          At Social Baluni Public School, academics is structured to inspire deep conceptual understanding rather than mechanical memorization. Affiliated with the Central Board of Secondary Education (CBSE), New Delhi, our pedagogy aligns with the National Education Policy (NEP 2020), blending activity-based inquiry in foundational stages with disciplined national entrance readiness in senior secondary years.
        </p>
        <div class="pt-2 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
          <Button href="/academics/integrated-programme/" variant="primary" size="md">
            Integrated NEET/JEE/NDA
          </Button>
          <Button href="/academics/day-boarding/" variant="outline" size="md">
            Day Boarding Schedule
          </Button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-lg border border-paper-300">
        <img
          src="/images/student-presentation-1280.webp"
          alt="Science practicals in composite laboratory"
          class="w-full h-full object-cover max-h-[380px]"
        />
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- The 5 Educational Stages -->
    <section class="space-y-8">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-crimson-900 border-b border-paper-300 pb-2">
        Academic Stages (Nursery to Class XII)
      </h2>

      <div class="space-y-6">
        <!-- 1. Foundational -->
        <div class="p-6 rounded-xl bg-paper-50 border border-paper-300 shadow-sm flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-6">
          <div class="w-16 h-16 rounded-xl bg-crimson-50 text-crimson-800 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-xl shrink-0">
            N–KG
          </div>
          <div class="space-y-2">
            <h3 class="font-serif text-xl font-bold text-paper-900">Foundational Stage (Nursery, LKG, UKG)</h3>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-paper-700 leading-relaxed">
              Joyful, play-based exploration focused on phonics, fine motor development, social communication, emotional security, and sensory discovery. Hands-on learning corners and story-based education ensure a gentle and enthusiastic transition into school life.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- 2. Primary / XSEED -->
        <div class="p-6 rounded-xl bg-paper-50 border border-paper-300 shadow-sm flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-6">
          <div class="w-16 h-16 rounded-xl bg-forest-50 text-forest-800 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-xl shrink-0">
            I–V
          </div>
          <div class="space-y-2">
            <h3 class="font-serif text-xl font-bold text-paper-900">Preparatory & Primary Stage (Classes I–V) — XSEED Method</h3>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-paper-700 leading-relaxed">
              Implemented through the globally acclaimed <strong>XSEED experiential methodology</strong>. Students do not simply listen to lectures; they experience concepts through tangible experiments, analyse findings, articulate observations, and apply knowledge to daily life scenarios.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- 3. Middle -->
        <div class="p-6 rounded-xl bg-paper-50 border border-paper-300 shadow-sm flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-6">
          <div class="w-16 h-16 rounded-xl bg-saffron-50 text-paper-900 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-xl shrink-0">
            VI–VIII
          </div>
          <div class="space-y-2">
            <h3 class="font-serif text-xl font-bold text-paper-900">Middle School Stage (Classes VI–VIII)</h3>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-paper-700 leading-relaxed">
              Structured transitions into specialized subjects: Physics, Chemistry, Biology, Mathematics, Social Sciences, Computer Applications, and three languages (English, Hindi, Sanskrit). Integrated mental ability and Olympiad foundation classes develop competitive logical reasoning.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- 4. Secondary -->
        <div class="p-6 rounded-xl bg-paper-50 border border-paper-300 shadow-sm flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-6">
          <div class="w-16 h-16 rounded-xl bg-crimson-100 text-crimson-900 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-xl shrink-0">
            IX–X
          </div>
          <div class="space-y-2">
            <h3 class="font-serif text-xl font-bold text-paper-900">Secondary Stage (Classes IX–X)</h3>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-paper-700 leading-relaxed">
              Rigorous preparation for CBSE All India Secondary School Examinations (AISSE). Early foundation batches begin for NTSE, JEE, NEET, and NDA, laying deep conceptual groundwork in high-school mathematics and basic sciences.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- 5. Senior Secondary -->
        <div class="p-6 rounded-xl bg-paper-50 border border-paper-300 shadow-sm flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-6">
          <div class="w-16 h-16 rounded-xl bg-forest-100 text-forest-900 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-xl shrink-0">
            XI–XII
          </div>
          <div class="space-y-2">
            <h3 class="font-serif text-xl font-bold text-paper-900">Senior Secondary Stage (Classes XI–XII)</h3>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-paper-700 leading-relaxed">
              Specialized streams in Medical (PCB), Engineering (PCM), Commerce, and Humanities. Synchronised classroom timetables integrate entrance coaching by Baluni Classes faculty for NEET and JEE Main/Advanced, as well as the Doon Baluni Defence Academy officer wing.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- XSEED 5-Step Learning Loop (From legacy what-is-xseed.md) -->
    <section class="bg-paper-50 p-8 sm:p-12 rounded-2xl border border-paper-300 space-y-8">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-crimson-900">
          The XSEED 5-Step Experiential Learning Cycle
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-paper-700">
          How our primary students master concepts by doing, questioning, and reflecting:
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-5 gap-4">
        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-paper-100 border border-paper-300 text-center space-y-2">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-crimson-700 text-white font-bold text-xs flex items-center justify-center mx-auto">1</div>
          <div class="font-serif font-bold text-sm text-paper-900">Aim</div>
          <p class="text-[11px] text-paper-600">Clarify the explicit learning goal and concept question before starting.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-paper-100 border border-paper-300 text-center space-y-2">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-crimson-700 text-white font-bold text-xs flex items-center justify-center mx-auto">2</div>
          <div class="font-serif font-bold text-sm text-paper-900">Action</div>
          <p class="text-[11px] text-paper-600">Conduct a hands-on activity, tangible experiment, or role play.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-paper-100 border border-paper-300 text-center space-y-2">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-crimson-700 text-white font-bold text-xs flex items-center justify-center mx-auto">3</div>
          <div class="font-serif font-bold text-sm text-paper-900">Analysis</div>
          <p class="text-[11px] text-paper-600">Discuss findings, question outcomes, and derive underlying principles.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-paper-100 border border-paper-300 text-center space-y-2">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-crimson-700 text-white font-bold text-xs flex items-center justify-center mx-auto">4</div>
          <div class="font-serif font-bold text-sm text-paper-900">Application</div>
          <p class="text-[11px] text-paper-600">Solve real-world problems and write exercises independently.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-paper-100 border border-paper-300 text-center space-y-2">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-crimson-700 text-white font-bold text-xs flex items-center justify-center mx-auto">5</div>
          <div class="font-serif font-bold text-sm text-paper-900">Assessment</div>
          <p class="text-[11px] text-paper-600">Evaluate conceptual retention with targeted feedback and reflection.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
